</div>
<div id="p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="p2.1" class="ltx_p"><em id="p2.1.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Keywords</em> Large Language Models  <math id="p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math>
Personalization  <math id="p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math>
Memory  <math id="p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math>
Text Generation  <math id="p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\cdot" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo>⋅</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\cdot</annotation></semantics></math>
Recommendation</p>
</div>
<figure id="S0.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2502.11528v2/Illustration.png" id="S0.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:476/154;" width="476" height="154" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 1: </span> Comparison of General LLM vs. Personalized LLM. Different users have different preferences. General LLMs fail to satisfy diverse needs with a one-size-fits-all approach, demonstrating the necessity for personalized LLMs.</figcaption>
</figure>
